config CACHE_NXP_LLC
	bool "NXP CodaCache last-level cache driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_NXP_LLC_ENABLED
	depends on EXTERNAL_CACHE
	select CACHE_HAS_DRIVER
	help
	  Enable the NXP CodaCache last-level cache (LLC) backend. This single
	  drivers/cache backend serves BOTH cache levels behind Zephyr's
	  level-less cache API: the CPU L1 (through the CMSIS SCB helpers) and
	  the CodaCache LLC in front of the external-memory windows. Selecting
	  EXTERNAL_CACHE removes the arch Cortex-M L1 backend
	  (arch/arm/core/cortex_m/cache.c, gated on ARCH_CACHE) from the build,
	  so this driver must cover both levels.

	  DMA buffers must not be placed in the LLC-cached aliases. See the
	  placement rule and its reasons in drivers/cache/cache_nxp_llc.c.
